{
 "duration": 51.059,
 "sentences": [
  {
   "index": 0,
   "start": 0.25,
   "end": 6.44,
   "text": "Go's JSON package has been quietly hiding bugs for years. Go 1.27 finally fixes it."
  },
  {
   "index": 1,
   "start": 6.84,
   "end": 9.483,
   "text": "Meet json/v2, now generally available."
  },
  {
   "index": 2,
   "start": 9.863,
   "end": 18.982,
   "text": "Problem one. The old package matched field names case insensitively. So a wrong key could silently fill your field. V2 needs an exact match."
  },
  {
   "index": 3,
   "start": 19.362,
   "end": 25.15,
   "text": "Problem two. Duplicate keys. V1 silently accepted them. V2 returns an error."
  },
  {
   "index": 4,
   "start": 25.53,
   "end": 31.654,
   "text": "Problem three. A nil slice was written as null, and broke your front end. V2 writes an empty array."
  },
  {
   "index": 5,
   "start": 32.034,
   "end": 36.455,
   "text": "It's also faster. Early benchmarks report decoding around twice as fast."
  },
  {
   "index": 6,
   "start": 36.835,
   "end": 43.496,
   "text": "The best part? Your old imports still work. The classic package now runs on the new engine, with the old behavior."
  },
  {
   "index": 7,
   "start": 43.896,
   "end": 50.159,
   "text": "So upgrade, then move to v2 one package at a time. Strict by default beats surprising by default."
  }
 ],
